CORE no-new-smt
pseudo-encodings.i
--arch x86_64 --os linux --floatbv --no-simplify
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Non-canonical x86 80-bit extended encodings: pseudo-NaN, pseudo-infinity, and
unnormals are NaN, and a pseudo-denormal has the value 2^-16382 *
1.fraction, as on x87 hardware.  pseudo-encodings-simplify.desc runs the same
test with the simplifier, which constant-folds the values built with constant
initialisers through ieee_float_valuet; both must agree.  The new SMT2 back end
(--incremental-smt2-solver) does not yet implement the byte-extract lowering
that the union accesses require.
